<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse in one column; page number at top right; gathering signature at foot.</layout>
  <page_number>185</page_number>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>Aa 2</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Autumnus amplo pallidus ubere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Irages colonis fuderit, &amp; suos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Pomona fructus legerit, heu, rigens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Tristi recurret Bruma vice. Heu, nives</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Per arua densa, Sarmatico &amp; gelu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Astricta passim flumina nos focum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Seruare cogent. Linque domum &amp; libros,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Quid inquieta sollicitudine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Mentem fatigas semper, &amp; hostium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Horrescis astus multiplices? Licet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Quandoque Musa decutere anxia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Seueriorum tadia frontibus:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Atque aegra curis pectora edacibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Leuare honestis risibus, &amp; locis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Quos casta Pallas, quos Citharaparens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Phoebus sonora diligat, &amp; Pudor.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>At quaeris hortus quo sit us est loco</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Quoque urbe distat passibus. An via</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Longinqua tardo fit nimium seni?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Et quae sit illi forma? Loquaciter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Haec cuncta dicet Musa. Palatij</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Vicina plani prata videt, suum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Quà mane Titan igniuomus diem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Terris redonat: Quà medios micat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Emensus axes lucidior, potest</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Torrentis Arua cernere concitos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Cursus, &amp; undis turbidam arenulis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Ripam. Volucris sed Rhodani placens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Audire gaudet murmur, equus vagas</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The printed page number is set at the top right and reads 185. The ampersand-like sign is printed as "&amp;". Several words in the italic verse are uncertain at line ends, notably "Irages", "Horrescis" and "sit us est", and are given as printed without marks because the scan is only partly legible.</notes>
</page>
